{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09d27a55e23f0042ba096ed63e33a748cb4e944e664ac5e7d437375198cfe694","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar doctor mapping-config diagnostics","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","mapping_config.load_mapping_config","MappingConfigError","mapping_probe.build_probe","config.projects","effective_status_map","effective_type_map","assert_type_decisions_complete","effective_link_map","capability_installed","jira_datacenter","JIRA_PAT","resolve_jira_datacenter_settings","docs/user-guide.md"],"problem_keywords":["mapping config diagnostics","offline validation","live drift detection","jira datacenter integration","doctor command","portability"],"propositions":["Offline mapping config validation must detect load-time errors (non-integer hierarchy, malformed blocks) and resolve-time errors (out-of-vocabulary, unmapped-non-skipped values) via provider-neutral resolvers, surfacing each as error findings with verbatim MappingConfigError details and non-zero exit.","Empty projects blocks must surface as warning findings (not errors) to flag stubs.","Live drift detection must compare configured vs observed vocabulary (status, type, link) via the S8 probe reader when jira-datacenter is importable and credentials resolve, emitting one finding per axis divergence.","Live drift check must degrade gracefully when jira-datacenter extra is absent, PAT is empty, settings resolution fails, or probe times out (doctor-side timeout default 10s), folding all causes into a single unavailable finding with reason and success exit.","Mapping diagnostics must run offline-always with stdlib-only imports, keeping mapping findings in their own list separate from run_repair iteration to preserve blocking-edge contract.","Hierarchy divergence is excluded from live drift diff because Data Center probe never observes hierarchyLevel (Cloud-only field), while offline hierarchy validity is covered by load-time checks."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787762628867514001,"uuid":"e763cac3-fe23-4891-885d-59d7052c80fa"}